Portions of this software are derived from the Go standard library and are licensed
under the BSD 3-Clause licence rather than Apache-2.0; see LICENSE-go:

  ftoa_append.go  the float layout, with strconv's two-digit integer formatter
  pow10tab.go     strconv's table of powers of ten
  uscale.go       strconv's unrounded scaling, cut down to float64

The parsing algorithms, and the amd64 assembly that implements them, follow simdjson
(https://github.com/simdjson/simdjson) by Daniel Lemire, Geoff Langdale and
contributors, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. The conversion between
float64 and decimal follows Russ Cox, "Floating-Point Printing and Parsing Can Be Simple
And Fast", https://research.swtch.com/fp.
